    "summary": ```
    Australian Senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore announced her resignation from the Senate after discovering she has British citizenship by descent through her mother. She was unaware of her dual citizenship status, believing earlier advice from the British embassy suggested she was not eligible. Her mother, born in Singapore during a British colonial period, gained UK citizenship in 1983, which automatically passed to Kakoschke-Moore.

    She will request a high court referral to determine how her Senate vacancy will be filled, with a potential recount likely to elect Tim Storrer. Nick Xenophon, her party leader, expressed devastation at her departure but believes this is not the end of her political career. The situation is considered legally complex due to recent high court decisions involving citizenship eligibility.
    ```,
    "key_details": {
        "reason_for_resignation": "Dual British citizenship",
        "citizenship_origin": "Mother's British citizenship by colonial descent",
        "potential_replacement": "Tim Storrer",
        "party": "Nick Xenophon Team"
    }
}

